---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const effectiveDate = "January 2, 2026";
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy | Daniel Black Applications" description="Privacy policy for applications by Daniel Black">
  <main class="relative z-10 min-h-screen">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-16">
      <header class="mb-12">
        <h1 class="font-display text-4xl md:text-5xl text-brand mb-4">Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="text-text-secondary">Effective Date: {effectiveDate}</p>
        <p class="text-text-tertiary mt-2">Applications by Daniel Black (danaucpe.org)</p>
      </header>

      <article class="prose prose-invert max-w-none space-y-8">

        <section class="bg-bg-secondary/50 rounded-xl p-6 border border-border-subtle">
          <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl text-text-primary mb-4">Overview</h2>
          <div class="p-4 bg-warning/10 border border-warning/30 rounded-lg mb-4">
            <p class="text-warning font-heading mb-2">Black Family Use Only</p>
            <p class="text-text-secondary">
              These applications are strictly for use by Daniel Black and members of the Black household.
              They are NOT public services and do not accept external users or account connections.
            </p>
          </div>
          <p class="text-text-secondary leading-relaxed">
            This privacy policy applies exclusively to personal applications developed by Daniel Black
            for private family use. These tools integrate with health and wellness services (such as
            Oura Ring) to provide personal insights. No data is shared with, sold to, or accessible
            by any third parties under any circumstances.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="bg-bg-secondary/50 rounded-xl p-6 border border-border-subtle">
          <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl text-text-primary mb-4">Data Access</h2>
          <p class="text-text-secondary leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Applications may access data through official APIs using OAuth 2.0 authentication with read-only permissions where applicable. Data accessed may include:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-text-secondary space-y-2 ml-4">
            <li>Health and wellness metrics (sleep, activity, heart rate, readiness scores)</li>
            <li>Basic account identifiers (email, user ID)</li>
            <li>Summary statistics and trends</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-text-tertiary mt-4 text-sm">
            No GPS location data, payment information, or sensitive credentials are collected.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="bg-bg-secondary/50 rounded-xl p-6 border border-border-subtle">
          <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl text-text-primary mb-4">Purpose of Use</h2>
          <p class="text-text-secondary leading-relaxed">
            Data is used exclusively for personal wellness insights, trend analysis, and integration
            with personal AI assistants and productivity tools.
          </p>
          <div class="mt-4 p-4 bg-bg-tertiary rounded-lg border border-border-subtle">
            <p class="text-brand font-heading">
              No data is sold, shared with third parties, or used for marketing purposes.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="bg-bg-secondary/50 rounded-xl p-6 border border-border-subtle">
          <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl text-text-primary mb-4">Storage & Retention</h2>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-text-secondary space-y-2 ml-4">
            <li>Data is stored locally or in private, encrypted storage systems</li>
            <li>Aggregated summaries may be retained for trend analysis</li>
            <li>Raw data is typically retained for 30-90 days unless otherwise specified</li>
            <li>Black family members may request deletion of their data at any time</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="bg-bg-secondary/50 rounded-xl p-6 border border-border-subtle">
          <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl text-text-primary mb-4">Security</h2>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-text-secondary space-y-2 ml-4">
            <li>All API communications use encrypted OAuth 2.0 channels</li>
            <li>No passwords or authentication credentials are stored</li>
            <li>Access tokens are securely managed and can be revoked at any time</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="bg-bg-secondary/50 rounded-xl p-6 border border-border-subtle">
          <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl text-text-primary mb-4">Family Member Rights</h2>
          <p class="text-text-secondary leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Black family members may revoke access to their data at any time by:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-text-secondary space-y-2 ml-4">
            <li>Revoking app permissions through the connected service's settings (e.g., Oura app)</li>
            <li>Contacting Daniel directly to request data deletion</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="bg-bg-secondary/50 rounded-xl p-6 border border-border-subtle">
          <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl text-text-primary mb-4">Contact</h2>
          <p class="text-text-secondary leading-relaxed">
            For questions about this privacy policy or to request data deletion, contact Daniel Black:
          </p>
          <p class="mt-4">
            <a href="https://x.com/danblack" class="text-brand hover:text-brand-light transition-colors">
              @danblack on X/Twitter
            </a>
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="bg-bg-secondary/50 rounded-xl p-6 border border-border-subtle">
          <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl text-text-primary mb-4">Changes to This Policy</h2>
          <p class="text-text-secondary leading-relaxed">
            This privacy policy may be updated from time to time. The effective date at the top
            of this page indicates when the policy was last revised.
          </p>
        </section>

      </article>

      <footer class="mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-border-subtle">
        <a href="/" class="text-brand hover:text-brand-light transition-colors font-heading">
          ← Back to Daemon
        </a>
      </footer>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
